{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "2026-10-16T06:55:53.413472+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-16T06:55:54.154610+00:00", "id": 23411227, "conceptrecid": "23411226", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23411226", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "metadata": {"title": "An explicit rank-two entropy-minimizing Fano degeneration", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "publication_date": "2026-10-16", "description": "<p>We give an explicit smooth Fano fivefold whose unique global Han\u2013Li entropy-minimizing valuation has rational rank two and is therefore nondivisorial. Its canonical first central variety is singular, so this first degeneration is nontrivial. The example is the product of Miao\u2013Wang's established quadric-blowup threefold with the first Hirzebruch surface. Exact moment equations specify the two positive weights. A universal resultant argument and the classical Hermite\u2013Lindemann theorem prove that their ratio is irrational. The associated graded anticanonical ring, canonical weight normalization, weak product soliton equation, and application of the established global optimality criterion are made explicit.</p><p>The construction satisfies the request discussed by Blum in Oberwolfach Report 17/2022, pp. 888\u2013889, without a dimension bound or a product exclusion. Major inputs are due to Miao\u2013Wang, Wang\u2013Zhu, Han\u2013Li, and Blum\u2013Liu\u2013Xu\u2013Zhuang. Earlier nontrivial first centers of Li\u2013Li are credited; their second example's rational rank was not certified in the sources inspected. The threefold factor was already announced in Miao\u2013Wang's January 2024 preprint. No novelty, historical firstness, exhaustive priority, or continued-openness certificate is claimed.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in developing, checking, and preparing the work. The reported adversarial reviews were performed by AI agents. This is an unrefereed preprint; independent human peer review and formal verification have not been completed. The accompanying verification archive preserves original proof and correction bytes, source fingerprints, bounded priority audits, adversarial analyses, and exact auxiliary diagnostics. Passing software checks does not formally verify the geometric or analytic theorem inputs.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["Fano varieties", "canonical degeneration", "K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci soliton", "entropy-minimizing valuation", "nondivisorial valuation", "rational rank two", "AI-assisted mathematics", "unrefereed preprint"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/888", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0.0", "references": ["H. Blum, Degenerations of unstable Fano varieties and Kahler\u2013Ricci soliton, in Toric Geometry, Oberwolfach Rep. 19 (2022), no. 2, Report 17/2022, pp. 888\u2013889; published online 14 April 2023. doi:10.4171/OWR/2022/17.", "M. Miao and L. Wang, Optimal Degenerations of K-unstable Fano threefolds, first posted 25 January 2024; cited edition arXiv:2401.13999v2, 13 April 2026.", "Y. Li and Z. Li, Equivariant R-test configurations and semistable limits of Q-Fano group compactifications, Peking Math. J. 6 (2023), 559\u2013607. doi:10.1007/s42543-022-00054-0. Inspected example text: arXiv:2103.06439v6.", "X.-J. Wang and X. Zhu, K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci solitons on toric manifolds with positive first Chern class, Adv. Math. 188 (2004), 87\u2013103. doi:10.1016/j.aim.2003.09.009.", "J. Han and C. Li, Algebraic uniqueness of K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci flow limits and optimal degenerations of Fano varieties, Geom. Topol. 28 (2024), 539\u2013592. Cited theorem numbering: arXiv:2009.01010v1.", "J. Han and C. Li, On the Yau\u2013Tian\u2013Donaldson conjecture for generalized K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci soliton equations, Comm. Pure Appl. Math. 76 (2023), 1793\u20131867. doi:10.1002/cpa.22053. Corollary 31 and Proposition 32 refer to the inspected author manuscript, https://sites.math.rutgers.edu/~cl1412/papers/g-soliton.pdf.", "H. Blum, Y. Liu, C. Xu and Z. Zhuang, The existence of the K\u00e4hler\u2013Ricci soliton degeneration, Forum Math. Pi 11 (2023), e9. doi:10.1017/fmp.2023.5. Inspected preprint: arXiv:2103.15278v2."], "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23411226"}}]}}, "title": "An explicit rank-two entropy-minimizing Fano degeneration", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23411227", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23411227", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23411227?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23411227", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23411227/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23411226", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23411226", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23411226", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23411226", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23411227/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23411227/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23411227/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23411227/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23411227:rank-two-fano-note.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23411227:rank-two-fano-note.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23411227:rank-two-fano-note.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/